# Firework EntertAInment Project Rules

- Use British English, straight apostrophes, and no em dashes.
- Treat the live local repo as the source of truth. Inspect files before
  answering or editing.
- Keep unrelated dirty worktree changes intact.
- Vercel deploys from `platform`.
- The app is ShowCrafter: a consumer firework show-planning platform for
  pyromusical shows built from retail catalogue items.
- Do not collapse upload-scoped music analysis into final show creation.
  Upload can start analysis; Generate creates the show and starts cue
  generation.
- Do not expose hidden background processing in UI copy unless an error blocks
  the user.
- Default cue generation is the fast deterministic planner. OpenRouter cue
  assignment is optional and selected through generation settings or
  `CUE_GENERATION_MODE=llm`.
- Keep generation controls truthful to the active mode. Show model selection
  only for `llm`; revalidate the mode on final Generate because settings can
  change while the wizard is open.
- Show cues are stored as `show_timeline_items`, not legacy `show_cues`.
- Upload-scoped analysis rows are `song_analyses`, not legacy
  `music_analyses`.
- The AI credit ledger reserves before cost-bearing work, settles on success,
  and refunds expected failures.
- Replacing or clearing uploaded music must use the guarded unused-analysis
  cleanup path. Refund only active unfinished work, charge completed analysis,
  and never discard an analysis already claimed by a show.
- Public browse access for catalogue/templates is intentional only for the
  documented tables and must be backed by explicit RLS policies.
- `/catalogue`, `/library`, and `/library/[id]` remain guest-accessible. Use
  public chrome for guests and workspace chrome for signed-in users.
- Explore presets come only from `show_presets`; do not append code-owned seed
  files. Create and import them as drafts, and publish only canonical catalogue
  cue UUIDs that fit within the duration without same-position overlap.
- Keep `source_show_id` for imported-preset provenance and idempotency. Show
  it only in admin projections and grants. Show real authenticated likes and
  public aggregate counts, never fabricated popularity numbers. Shelf labels
  and See all results must match their real predicate and full result set. See
  `platform/docs/explore-presets.md`.
- Filter admin navigation by each route's real permission. Navigation hiding is
  not authorisation, so enforce the same permission on routes and actions.
- Destructive and password-reset UI must run the stated Supabase Auth action.
  Build reset redirects from `APP_ORIGIN`, never request host headers. Do not
  report success for a placeholder or profile-only substitute.
- Preserve editor changes made during an in-flight save, include every
  simulation input in replay cache keys, keep physical ranges non-negative,
  and label the actual slider thumb. See `platform/docs/editor-integrity.md`.
- Apply schema changes through chronological migrations, regenerate database
  types, and pair RLS with explicit least-privilege Data API and RPC grants.
- Run the narrowest useful verification for the change and state clearly when a
  full gate was not run.

## Main Commands

```bash
cd platform
npm run dev
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm test
npm run build
npm run check
```

Python analyser tests:

```bash
cd platform/analyser
python -m unittest discover -s tests -p "*test*.py"
```

Import worker:

```bash
cd platform
npm run worker:firework-import
```
